# The upstream base of this source fork and the upstream content that
# scripts/scan.sh accepts. See docs/secret-handling.md, "Upstream content".
#
# Format: one entry for each line, fields separated by one tab. A line that
# starts with "#" is a comment.
#   tag<TAB><tag><TAB><commit>
#       The upstream release tag of the last merge into local-dev and its
#       commit (40 hex digits). A ref refs/upstream/tags/<tag> must point to
#       this commit. Change the line in the merge of a new upstream tag, then
#       run "scripts/scan.sh baseline" and replace this file with its output.
#   archive<TAB><blob><TAB><path>
#       An upstream file that the policy check "archive" accepts: the exact
#       Git blob id and path. Write the reason in a comment above it.
#   hit<TAB><line hash><TAB><path>
#       Generated by "scripts/scan.sh baseline": a line of the base tree that
#       a tracked host-value rule finds (the Git blob id of the line and the
#       path). The scan uses these lines only when the base commit is not in
#       the repository (a shallow clone). No rule of .local/host-values.deny
#       goes into this file.
